cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  fieldspice: first-principles electromagnetic field simulation
  for analog and digital circuits
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hou
    given-names: Steven
repository-code: https://github.com/Steve8323/fieldspice
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-08-05'
keywords:
  - electromagnetics
  - quasistatic
  - finite integration technique
  - drift-diffusion
  - TCAD
  - parasitic extraction
  - signal integrity
  - circuit simulation
  - electrothermal
abstract: >-
  A field solver for the regime full-wave FDTD cannot reach: structures far
  smaller than a wavelength, filled with conductors and semiconductors, driven
  for microseconds rather than picoseconds. Discretising Maxwell's equations in
  integrated variables on a Yee grid makes the discrete gradient, curl and
  divergence exact signed-incidence matrices, so curl-grad and div-curl vanish
  identically and all metric information collapses into diagonal mass matrices
  that are ordinary circuit elements. A field region is therefore literally an
  RLC network, which makes exact field-circuit coupling a matter of assembly
  rather than interpolation. Dropping radiation removes the Courant limit and
  buys four to ten orders of magnitude in step count. Includes
  electroquasistatic, frequency-domain, drift-diffusion, heat-conduction and
  coupled electro-thermal solvers, a SPICE engine, parasitic extraction, and a
  full-wave solver retained specifically so the quasi-static approximation can
  be checked rather than trusted.
